## Hunt the Wumpus's claims: what the cave at the test seed can reach, each
## under the rooms, things and verbs that are load-bearing on the way. The
## test tree's manifest names this file; the story never imports it.
##
## At seed 42 the hunter wakes in the Shambles, the wumpus sleeps in the Drum
## and the pit is in the Cistern. Neither hazard room is in any set below, so
## a held claim is a proof that the walk never had to stand in one: the game
## is won by deduction, not by going and looking (docs/cave-map.md).

claims
  needs rooms: the Shambles, the Dead Well, the Rookery, the Gullet, the Deep
  needs things: the bow, the note
  needs verbs: north, south, east, west, southeast, northwest, shoot north, shoot east, shoot west

  claim the wumpus can be killed without entering a hazard
    the story ends in victory

  claim the first blood is taught on the way
    the story is warned
end claims
